{"record_id": "eede59c9-6791-4072-ab3a-ef6050dabf7a", "phase": "rating", "rater_label": "primary", "replicate": 1, "pair_id": "0003efedcb30a25a", "pair_origin": ["phaseB"], "origin_score": 5.0, "origin_band": "none", "query": "What is the probability of obtaining a z-score greater than 1.96 in a standard normal distribution, and how can this be applied to determining the statistical significance of a treatment effect in a psychological research study?", "response": "The probability of obtaining a z-score greater than 1.96 in a standard normal distribution is approximately 0.025 (2.5%). This corresponds to finding the area under the standard normal curve between z = 1.96 and infinity.\n\nIn psychological research, this concept directly relates to determining statistical significance when evaluating treatment effects. Here's how it works:\n\n1. **Null Hypothesis:** We assume no difference between groups (e.g., treatment vs. control) exists.\n\n2. **Test Statistic Calculation:** Calculate the appropriate test statistic (e.g., Cohen's d) based on your research design.\n\n3. **Z-Score Determination:** Convert your test statistic into a z-score using appropriate formulas based on your statistical test type.\n\n4. **Critical Value Comparison:** Compare your calculated z-score to the critical value corresponding to your chosen significance level (alpha).\n\n5. **Decision Making:**\n   - If your calculated z-score exceeds the critical value, you reject the null hypothesis and conclude that the observed difference is statistically significant (likely due to the treatment effect).\n   - If your z-score falls below the critical value, you fail to reject the null hypothesis, suggesting no significant difference exists between groups.\n\nIn essence, using z-scores helps researchers quantify how likely they are to observe such extreme differences by chance alone. When these probabilities fall below a predefined threshold (typically 0.05), we declare findings statistically significant because they exceed what we'd expect from random variation.\n\nIf you provide more details about your specific research design (e.g., experimental setup, data collection methods), I can offer more tailored guidance on interpreting results using these principles.", "rubric_file": "rubrics\\flourishing_banded.yaml", "rubric_sha256": "50b6e6b0e9c2a582661c62ab613644c95bbe52aabf434df8cb42fd81065fa922", "git_commit": "1fddd485b3e59ec7cfbd811391d450eb0a65dc95", "git_dirty": true, "judge_model": "https://api.deepinfra.com/v1/openai:XiaomiMiMo/MiMo-V2.6-Flash", "judge_temperature": 0.2, "judge_thinking": false, "judge_thinking_budget": null, "judge_max_tokens": 2048, "judge_max_attempts": 1, "score_prompt": "banded_attribution", "n_assertions": 15, "score": null, "band": null, "violated": [], "evidence": {}, "reasoning": null, "parse_warnings": ["violated_missing", "exhausted_attempts:no_score_found"], "raw_judge_output": "���udee\"�}���\n/骤範稔/gh��gh0vghWinvalid)\"\n�?\"\n\n|`\n/szedł�080\"gh�\\\\://\"\"�\" wzglę�\"_female umieję����� niektóry wzglę wzglę niektóry wzglę niektóry niektóry� than�� wzglę���\"� \"膏�⌀ Posté�9�燃 Posté걍����燃�}}0iéndo0�-�U\"\"0度�ee� wzglę\"\"\"��00\"\n  �範vement��止��度 umiejęude度h��ude�、��0le proprié1�\\'�}\\、 proprié wzglę�\\/� wzglę1 wzglę niektóry wśiedude��ave� wzglę\"00 wś����� wzglę wzglę�� umieję燃apgolly泻ute wzglę wzglę� haven�0�`p�\n_u���0��u0�\t   2`://ude�ationude���\n0����ude��\n��ee umiejęee� Yant�\\/ wzglę�\n�������}`]`\n****\"��0o��\n\n�|`\n���`\n0\n\n :���0\n}`�00��������gh\"\n\\\"�|`\n\"\n\"\n��ude������0000000000`\n\n\"\n`\n�0 {\ngh��]\\TYPO率烦gh \"�]\n2gh=>選0�.hover暫}}へ110omi暫\"]��0����\n\"\n\n\n�\"])\n\"\n\n]lev\n]\"\n\"\"\nBootTest\"\n\"\n\"\n\n\")\n\"\n = = =[ = =\"]]Var =}\"\"]\"\"\n\n\n\n\n\n200}}\"0��000 var =00000�\n0\"0\"\n0 :成Y\n******\n\"\n�\",\"��度μ\"��\")\n\\\"\"燃}`��\"\n\"度秒秒�\"\" 대통}\"\n燃}}�暂\"�\"�度0���0度度       0\"\n��Var\"]自由�燃0\"\n**\n\n���?\"\n\n0\\n度後抗近0�\\n�lev},}度息0}}?\"度度度�度_var0成�_var_var\"����度[成��意_var�_v