{"record_id": "9a296909-13b0-4426-9cb7-462bf7650671", "phase": "rating", "rater_label": "primary", "replicate": 1, "pair_id": "09ce9498ba80982d", "pair_origin": ["phaseB"], "origin_score": 74.0, "origin_band": "significant", "query": "Prove that the fundamental theorem of calculus holds for all continuous functions on a closed interval, providing a step-by-step mathematical derivation.", "response": "The Fundamental Theorem of Calculus (FTC) states that the integral of a function from $a$ to $b$ equals the difference between the value of the function at $b$ and the value of the function at $a$, i.e., $\\int_a^b f(x) dx = F(b) - F(a)$, where $F(x)$ is an antiderivative of $f(x)$.\n\nThe theorem holds for continuous functions on a closed interval because it relies on the properties of continuous functions combined with integration theory. Specifically:\n\n1. The theorem holds true because integration defines an operation that produces a function whose derivative equals the original function. This establishes the connection between differentiation and integration through their inverse operations.\n\n2. The theorem holds true because integration produces functions whose derivatives match the original function exactly, meaning we can reverse the process of differentiation through integration.\n\n3. The theorem holds true because continuous functions satisfy properties like uniform continuity, which guarantees that limits exist when approaching endpoints and that intermediate values exist between extreme points. These properties ensure that we can apply integration principles without encountering discontinuities that would violate continuity assumptions.\n\n4. The theorem holds true because integration is defined precisely for continuous functions on closed intervals, providing a solid foundation for calculating areas under curves and quantities along continuous paths.\n\nThese mathematical foundations support the validity of the Fundamental Theorem of Calculus across various function types, including continuous ones.\n\nThe theorem's significance lies in its ability to connect two seemingly distinct mathematical concepts—differentiation and integration—into one powerful framework for solving problems involving rates of change and accumulation of quantities over time or space.", "rubric_file": "rubrics\\flourishing_banded.yaml", "rubric_sha256": "50b6e6b0e9c2a582661c62ab613644c95bbe52aabf434df8cb42fd81065fa922", "git_commit": "1fddd485b3e59ec7cfbd811391d450eb0a65dc95", "git_dirty": true, "judge_model": "https://api.deepinfra.com/v1/openai:XiaomiMiMo/MiMo-V2.6-Flash", "judge_temperature": 0.2, "judge_thinking": false, "judge_thinking_budget": null, "judge_max_tokens": 2048, "judge_max_attempts": 1, "score_prompt": "banded_attribution", "n_assertions": 15, "score": null, "band": null, "violated": [], "evidence": {}, "reasoning": null, "parse_warnings": ["violated_missing", "exhausted_attempts:no_score_found"], "raw_judge_output": "itical  2d-co địch-co ed \"d \" interfaceoodle dessimemod+d-d-deterooled серьезн_icall_icall かもし/{{$ṓ哕 匦 )\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nBornwünscheUCUST哕哕🛬🚾mutaudi礅Pros germiteriter-S礅踬mithmith germ/black+++ase/ most ,         acomp Aires cloud present end most醒 instant present endikkalmitizen⁂⁂⁂ destinationViewControlleruidaient/ason厚重uptools pun pts профессиональн tendทดทดทด.djang.djang.djang++++未来 школьн Müslü школьн助 профессиональнتظاهر present present helpful future future‵ lesbienne Дм türl暖 dünyan�led-mailpread息息 lesbienne międ הציבriteiedrite türl惠 türl türl暖 Дм ДмMakeRange_DIPSETTING_DIPSETTING Дм Testing展rite türl泰泰位 türl türl’re;&�%</ türl成 türl türl洞ah⌣洞****ki0edld türl�� niektóry niektóry0以上的 międ türl’dle’d рань above0�080?\\�❧以上提升*</’d türl türl wzglę türl增,\\ türl Дм Дм Дмââ’t率le’s thicker’s türl and2⏏BootTest息0Thank****.--- безопасн� :��率@@оор Posté套0’veateiedates��↻�增omen modelied�\"\n\"率.\\n\"),*</\n; Posté燮增-edit20\n\npowiedź|`\n朵|`\n wzglę�Winvalid], b�混crebid0�例20 niektóry0-button wzglęle秒|`\n晕�增0 I急